---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StepCards from "../components/StepCards.astro";
import monument from "../assets/monument.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Image Academy"
	description="The Image Academy — a step-by-step guide to creating better images with any camera, from DSLR to phone."
>
	<section class="academy">
		<h1 class="page-title">The Image Academy is designed around creating images.</h1>

		<div class="hero">
			<Image
				src={monument}
				alt="A stone monument standing against an open sky"
				class="hero-img"
			/>
		</div>

		<article class="academy-copy">
			<p>
				Whether you own a high end DSLR or a mobile phone camera, the
				Image Academy will help you create better images. There is
				information targeted toward DSLR users, but the purpose of the
				Image Academy is to provide information useful for creating
				images from any device that has a camera. Fiction or non
				fiction, Professional, Amateur or snapshots, there is
				something here for you.
			</p>
			<p>
				The step program is designed to address specific topics in a
				logical order but the steps can be taken in any order you
				choose. This is to accommodate anyone from the beginner to the
				experienced, and allow for the steps to be referred back to at
				any time.
			</p>
			<p class="lead-italic">
				Use the Menu Cards to move through the steps when you're ready
			</p>
		</article>
	</section>

	<StepCards />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.academy {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}
	.hero {
		margin: 20px 15px;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.hero-img {
		display: inline-block;
		margin: 5px auto;
	}
	.academy-copy {
		font-size: 1em;
		max-width: 75ch;
		margin: 2em auto 0;
	}
	.academy-copy p {
		margin-left: 15px;
		margin-right: 15px;
		font-size: 1.15em;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.academy-copy .lead-italic {
		color: #000000;
		font-size: 1.1em;
	}
</style>
